Package: Entropic.Scree
Title: Information-Theoretic Measurement Mapping and Rank Estimation
Version: 1.0.2
Authors@R: 
    person("Terrence J.", "Lee-St. John", , "terry@enli.com.au", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Copyright: Terrence J. Lee-St. John (Enli)
Description: Maps relationships among measurements using a double-centered,
    joint-entropy-normalized mutual information matrix. Provides informational-axis
    loadings, primary and extended spectral-boundary diagnostics, and spectral-volume
    and informational-gravity summaries for discrete and discretized tabular data.
    The selected Primary Informational Rank is a candidate information-spectrum
    boundary, not an identified generating dimension. Optional, explicitly
    recorded missing-data preparation supports categorical missing states and
    numeric median fills with protected missingness indicators.
    For methodological details, see Lee-St. John (2026)
    <doi:10.5281/zenodo.22028086>.
URL: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22028086
